error[3-0061]: `MemArray<SCell>` is state-only
   ┌─ state_only_memory_pointers.fe:16:10
   │
16 │ fn cells(_ cells: own MemArray<SCell>) {}
   │          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ a state-only type cannot be an `own` parameter
   │
   = `MemArray<SCell>` holds `SCell`, which is pinned to storage
   = a state-only type lives at its place in storage or transient storage; name it with an access, such as `let m = mut store.balances`, or pass it as a `mut` or view parameter

